Axn class-level schema reflection
  the nil axis across every validator axn accepts
    reads format without:, a regexp that matches the empty string the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads format without:, a regexp that matches anything the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads format with:, resolved per call the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads format, the bare shorthand ActiveModel reads as with: the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads inclusion, a set containing nil the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads inclusion, a Hash set keyed by nil the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads inclusion, a Hash set without a nil key the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads exclusion, a Hash set keyed by nil the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads exclusion, a Hash set without a nil key the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads inclusion, a set without nil the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads length, maximum only the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads length, a floor the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads length, a range the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads numericality the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads presence, true the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads presence, false the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads type that rejects nil the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads type that nil satisfies the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads of the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads shape the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads the emptiness check allow_empty: false installs the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads model: the way the runtime treats an omitted value
    reads a custom validate: as nil-rejecting, which is stricter than its runtime
    reaches ActiveModel's unknown-validator error for uniqueness:
  unrepresentable-subfield omission warning
    warns, naming the omitted field
    warns at most once per class across repeated input_schema calls
    does not warn for a representable deep chain (object-shaped parents)
    does not warn when every subfield is shallow
  emptiness constraints
    emits minItems for a required Array
    emits minProperties for a required Hash
    emits minLength for a required String
    omits the constraint when the field allows empty
    omits the constraint when the field is optional
    emits it for the may-be-nil-but-not-empty cell alongside a nullable type
    honors an author-declared length minimum
    emits nothing for a type with no empty state
    floors a :params field under allow_empty: false, which takes no default presence check
    leaves a :params field floorless under allow_empty: true
    every length: spelling that names a floor
      reads an exact size
      reads a range's lower bound
      reads ActiveModel's implicit floor for a blank-intolerant entry with no floor of its own
      falls back to the presence floor for a per-call minimum it cannot resolve
      falls back to the presence floor for an unemittable infinite minimum
      reads a bare Range shorthand under a gated type, which ActiveModel expands into a floor
      reads a bare Range shorthand under a nil-admitting type
      reads a bare Range shorthand identically wherever the entry reaches reflection normalized
      keeps the emptiness axis and the emitted floor agreeing on a bare shorthand
      carries no floor for a bare shorthand that names none, as ActiveModel names none either
      carries no fractional floor, which ActiveModel refuses as a bound anyway
      carries the flag's own floor when the author's floor has no whole size to carry
      emits no floor for a maximum that admits an empty value
    an entry a gate may skip
      emits the floor of a gated presence:, which a call may run
      emits the floor of a gated length:, which a call may run
    on a shaped type whose JSON type the shape establishes
      floors the object by its own key, with no key from the pre-shape type left behind
      carries an author-declared floor under that same key
      keeps a shaped Hash flooring exactly as it does without the shape
      keeps a shaped Array flooring by items count
      leaves an unshaped unmappable type on its permissive fallback
    on a union's anyOf branches
      floors every size-bearing branch of a required union
      leaves a branch with no empty state unconstrained
      floors no branch at all when the union tolerates blank
      never floors the nullability branch
    blank tolerance
      emits no floor for an explicit length minimum the field tolerates blank around
      emits no floor for a blank-tolerant presence check
      keeps the floor for allow_empty: false, whose own check is explicitly blank-intolerant
      a blank-tolerant length: alongside a check that rejects every empty value
        keeps the floor when the inferred presence check rejects the empty value
        keeps the floor when the emptiness check rejects the empty value
        keeps the floor when an explicit presence: rejects the empty value
        emits no floor when nothing else rejects the empty value
        emits no floor when the only other check is one that is switched off
    alongside an author-declared length: under a nil-tolerance
      floors a length: that only caps the size
      floors an explicitly disabled length:
      carries the author's own floor, which optional: alone would have dropped
      still drops the floor when allow_empty: is not declared at all
    on output_schema
      emits the floor for a required collection
      floors a union's branches outbound too
      omits the floor when a nested gate could skip the presence check that promises it

Axn semantic_hints
  defaults to an empty array
  stores validated core-vocabulary hints
  rejects unknown hints
  accepts adapter-registered vocabulary
  inherits hints and lets a subclass replace them

the unnamed-crossing seam (PRO-3068)
  returns the node a dotted tail crosses without naming it
  returns nil when the config anchors on that node by reader name
  returns nil for a top-level config, which reads no segment at all
  reports the anchor's own chain index for a dotted on:

Subfield read-path resolution runtime truth (PRO-2903)
  defaults
    resolves a nil-parent subfield default without materializing the parent
    materializes an absent Hash-typed parent
    refuses to materialize a non-object (type: Array) parent — the default is skipped, the parent stays nil
    does not overwrite a present subfield value
    fills a nil subfield value under a present parent
    applies default: false (kwarg parity: non-nil defaults apply, matching top-level semantics)
    instance_execs a Proc default against the action
    resolves a deep subfield default under a present parent without adding the intermediate
    resolves a deep subfield default under a nil parent without materializing the chain
    does not materialize the parent for interacting deep defaults under a nil parent
    resolves a default off an object parent without mutating it (no setter write-back)
  preprocess
    transforms a present subfield value
    drops the preprocess result when the parent is nil (never synthesizes the parent)
    does not mutate the caller's parent hash (simple key write-back is copy-on-write)
    does not mutate the caller's nested hash either (deep write-back is copy-on-write too)
    never contaminates a literal top-level default with one call's nested writes

Axn
  symbol key normalization (PRO-2790)
    read path — call-arg key vs declared-field key
      symbol field declaration
        works with a symbol call key
        works with a string call key (the **params trap)
      string field declaration
        works with a symbol call key
        works with a string call key
    write path — expose key vs declared-exposure key
      reads back a string-keyed positional expose against a string declaration
      reads back a string-keyed hash expose
      reads back a string expose_return_as
    declaration normalization
      symbolizes the wire key so config.field is always a symbol
      defines a symbol-named reader for a string declaration
      treats :note and "note" as the same field (duplicate)
      symbolizes exposes wire keys too

Axn::Core::Tagging
  .tag / .dimension declaration forms
    accepts a name + positional resolver
    accepts a name + block
    accepts a literal value
    symbolizes string names
    stores dimensions separately from tags
    defaults a facet to the inputs phase
    marks a facet as result phase with from: :result
    accepts from: with the block form
    raises for an unknown from: phase
    raises when positional args are not exactly a name/value pair
    raises when given a bare name with no resolver
    raises when given both a positional resolver and a block
    raises when given a block with no name
    rejects the removed symbol-key hash form
    rejects the removed hashrocket hash form
    does not expose the parser as a public class method
  .dimension declaration forms
    accepts a name + block
    marks a dimension as result phase with from: :result
  .coerce
    passes OpenTelemetry-legal scalars through unchanged
    stringifies a non-scalar value
    stringifies non-Integer/Float numerics (BigDecimal/Rational), which OpenTelemetry drops
    stringifies non-finite floats (NaN / Infinity), which OpenTelemetry rejects
